course: dictionary
lesson: 10822
title: A veil covers or hides
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A veil is a thin piece of cloth worn over the head or face. A bride may wear a white veil at her wedding. Beekeepers wear a veil too, as the sentence «Beekeepers wear a suit and veil and puff smoke at the hive» shows.
explain: Veil can also be a word for anything that covers or hides something. «The hills were hidden behind a veil of mist.» You cannot see the hills, because the mist covers them like a cloth would. Ask yourself: what is being hidden here?
explain: Veil can be a verb too, meaning to cover or hide something partly. «Clouds veiled the moon» means the clouds covered some of the moon, so it was not fully bright. A veiled threat is one that is hinted at, not said openly.
fact: A veil is a thin piece of cloth worn over the head or face.
fact: «Veil» can also mean something that covers or hides, like «a veil of mist» or «a veil of secrecy».
fact: «Veiled» means partly covered or hidden: «a veiled threat» is a hint of trouble, not a clear warning.
fact: In church, a nun wears a veil on her head, and when a woman becomes a nun, people say she «takes the veil».
fact: Phrases to know: «lift the veil» means reveal what was hidden, and «a veil of darkness» means dark that hides things.
exercise: «The bride walked down the aisle in a long white veil.» What is a veil? | A small boat | A type of flower | *A thin cloth worn over the head or face | Something that makes a loud noise
exercise: «The hills were hidden behind a veil of mist.» What does veil mean here? | A kind of tall tree | To shout loudly | Shining bright like a lamp | *Something that covers or hides
exercise: «The note made a veiled threat, hinting that trouble would come.» What does veiled mean here? | Written very neatly | *Hinted at, not said openly | Said loudly and clearly | Painted in bright colours
test: «Beekeepers wear a suit and veil.» What is the veil in this sentence? | *A thin cloth over the face | A kind of bee | A puff of smoke | A tall ladder
test: «Clouds veiled the moon, so the night was dim.» What does veiled mean here? | Moved quickly | Lit up | Made brighter | *Partly covered or hidden
exam: «The plan was kept behind a veil of secrecy.» What does veil of secrecy suggest? | *The plan was kept hidden | The plan was thrown away | The plan was shouted from the roof | The plan was about bees
